  "term": "collective unconscious",
  "definition": "The collective unconscious is a Jungian idea referring to deep, shared symbolic patterns in the human mind that shape themes such as fear, social bonding, and hierarchy beyond individual experience. In this source, it is described as an evolved psychological structure that developed gradually in human ancestry and later became evident in symbolic thought and expression.",
